What was learned about the world *outside* this repository — how an API really
behaves, a vendor's actual limit, why a library was rejected — belongs in
`{{ index .Caps "research.findings" }}/`. Look there before searching, and write what
you find there before the session ends.

Findings carry `question:`, `sources:` (URLs you opened), `confidence:` and
`expires:`. They expire on a date because research goes stale when the world moves,
which watching this repository can never detect. Never renew a date without
re-reading a source.
